part pit_15
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-15 · Business revenue. Under every PIT-10 form, and for SOC-4 .3 and .5, revenue counts on the invoice's issue day (.1), at its net price (.2); an invoice in florens is converted under GEN-4 with the issue day as the event (.3); under (c), a month's social contributions come off the part at the highest rate first, each part's base rounded, the tax the sum of base times rate, rounded (.4)."
  note "No figure: the households' revenue defs apply it."

source pit_15 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-15 Business revenue (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

version pit15_v1
  cite pit_15
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "PIT-15 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-09-01; governs tax years from 2018, advances for months from January 2018, SOC-4 contributions for months from January 2022."
